WEBVTT

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:04.570
Yeah, I saw. It's being torn down.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.430
What? You want to get the band back together?

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.860
Kurosaki-san's not playing rock anymore?

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:06.250
Impossible...

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:10.530
Is it true, Haruka?

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:17.620
When I was discussing his solo song with him...

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:21.680
What? Not a rock song?

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.640
Yeah. Make it something 
Idol Kurosaki Ranmaru would sing.

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:29.140
Okay, but why?

00:03:30.130 --> 00:03:31.580
Because I'm not playing rock anymore.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:32.900
You're not?

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:36.950
Right now, I'm focusing on QUARTET NIGHT.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:46.520
I don't believe it...

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:51.710
I heard Ranmaru-senpai was in a rock 
band before he joined Shining Agency.

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:55.540
Yes. He was the bassist in his band.

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:58.170
He still plays it all the time in his room.

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:00.630
It's so cool.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:04.090
But why would he suddenly stop?

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:13.600
Is it that easy to give up something you love?

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:14.500
What?

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:19.770
Wouldn't that be like 
Syo giving up "manliness?"

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:20.710
Me...

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:21.910
Giving up...

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:23.030
Manliness?

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:30.060
It's impossible.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:30.930
It's impossible.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:31.810
Impossible.

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:32.930
It's impossible.

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:34.540
It's definitely impossible.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.420
I'm not sure I'm happy about this...

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:40.420
But that's what makes you great.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:46.050
Well, it's definitely hard 
to give up something you love.

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.620
You're right.

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:51.560
Maru-chan-senpai absolutely loves rock.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:54.030
It'll be fine, Nanami.

00:04:54.030 --> 00:04:57.190
I look forward to hearing 
Ranmaru-senpai's solo song.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:04:59.000
Okay.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:07.010
<i>Not a rock song, huh?</i>

00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:08.090
I can't do it.

00:05:09.720 --> 00:05:10.600
I'm sorry.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:14.200
I can't miss work.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:18.220
I appreciate the invitation.

00:05:18.900 --> 00:05:20.200
But I've made up my mind.

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.050
I'm not playing rock any—

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:26.910
Who's there? Show yourself.

00:05:31.960 --> 00:05:33.060
You...

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.310
I-I'm sorry.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:37.520
I didn't mean to eavesdrop...

00:05:38.050 --> 00:05:40.350
It wasn't anything important.

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:42.560
It was from an old friend.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:44.300
An old friend?

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.740
You mean from your band days?

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:52.970
Did you know they're tearing down 
the outdoor stage in the park?

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:58.530
Y-Yes. They're building 
the Triple S Stadium there, right?

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:03.100
They're holding one last rock festival there.

00:06:03.100 --> 00:06:05.600
An old friend asked if I'd play with him.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.470
It'd be a one-night-only reunion.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:09.610
That's amazing!

00:06:09.610 --> 00:06:12.430
When is it? I'll definitely go see it!

00:06:12.430 --> 00:06:13.760
I turned him down.

00:06:14.070 --> 00:06:14.820
What?

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:16.480
I have work that day.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:19.340
Besides, I don't play rock anymore.

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:20.550
B-But...

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:21.180
What?

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:29.210
Do you really have to give up what you love 
to be an idol of QUARTET NIGHT?

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:38.630
I can't handle two jobs at once.

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:08.870
You're too soft, Jinguji.

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:10.820
You have to—

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:12.130
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:14.460 --> 00:07:16.030
Kurosaki-san's bass is missing!

00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:21.830
What's going on, Ran-chan?

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:25.380
Are you really giving up rock?

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:27.760
Shut up.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:28.880
Just go to bed.

00:07:31.270 --> 00:07:33.640
Okay, let's take a break.

00:07:40.260 --> 00:07:42.840
Today's dance lessons are rough.

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:55.820
Ran-Ran's really into it.

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:59.260
His movements are 1.25 
times sharper than normal.

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:03.500
Has he finally learned to love QUARTET NIGHT?

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:05.830
What a ridiculous fantasy.

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:08.590
Myu-chan, you're so mean.

00:08:09.050 --> 00:08:12.050
It may be more than a fantasy.

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:12.820
What?

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:18.970
Ranmaru said he'd give up rock 
to focus on QUARTET NIGHT.

00:08:19.800 --> 00:08:21.430
Give up rock?

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:06.270
Ran-chan seems serious about this.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:07.320
What?

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:08.680
Serious?

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:09.950
You mean...

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:13.280
Yes. He seems serious about giving up rock.

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:18.220
He's been putting a lot of energy 
into dance lessons and stamina training.

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:21.450
We've seen it, too.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:24.810
Cecil-kun, Tokiya-kun, Otoya-kun.

00:09:24.810 --> 00:09:26.830
What did you see?

00:09:27.410 --> 00:09:31.440
Ranmaru-senpai doing dance lessons 
in the middle of the night.

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:34.690
There's nothing strange about him practicing.

00:09:34.690 --> 00:09:37.350
If anything, it's what he 
should do as a professional.

00:09:37.350 --> 00:09:38.180
But...

00:09:38.690 --> 00:09:39.430
But?

00:09:39.650 --> 00:09:42.430
It seemed like he was trying 
to forget something.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:47.940
He's forcing himself to train, 
so he can forget his feelings for rock?

00:09:48.390 --> 00:09:49.210
Yes...

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:56.200
He put his bass away 
and hasn't even tried to touch it.

00:09:56.970 --> 00:09:59.660
He used to play it every day.

00:09:59.960 --> 00:10:01.350
I'm worried.

00:10:12.850 --> 00:10:15.630
All-nighters are rough.

00:10:16.150 --> 00:10:18.600
Are you sure you're not just weak?

00:10:18.600 --> 00:10:21.500
I meant on my skin.

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:24.990
I need to take care of it before I go to sleep.

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:28.380
I know. Want me to do yours, too?

00:10:28.380 --> 00:10:30.980
Ringo's special skin care.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:36.570
Is that Kurosaki?

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.470
He's up so early...

00:10:38.470 --> 00:10:39.700
Hey, Kurosaki!

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:45.830
Good morning.

00:10:46.070 --> 00:10:47.850
Morning!

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:50.380
You're working hard this morning.

00:10:50.380 --> 00:10:51.250
Not really...

00:10:54.690 --> 00:10:55.170
Later.

00:10:55.390 --> 00:10:56.210
Kurosaki!

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:01.130
You seem tired.

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:03.950
Training too hard isn't good for your body.

00:11:03.950 --> 00:11:04.880
Yes, sir.

00:11:04.880 --> 00:11:07.180
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:11:07.180 --> 00:11:10.440
Taking care of yourself is part of your job.

00:11:11.020 --> 00:11:11.730
Yes, sir.

00:11:18.640 --> 00:11:21.480
He didn't seem like himself.

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:22.710
Is he all right?

00:12:53.650 --> 00:12:56.090
<i>I hope we get to play here someday.</i>

00:12:56.940 --> 00:13:00.170
<i>We'll fill this place with fans.</i>

00:13:01.170 --> 00:13:02.630
<i>Yeah, someday.</i>

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:04.680
<i>Someday we will!</i>

00:13:09.930 --> 00:13:13.260
Why? Why?

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:15.490
Senpai...

00:13:15.490 --> 00:13:16.370
Why?

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:17.570
Kurosaki-senpai...

00:13:17.570 --> 00:13:18.360
Why?

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:19.860
Kurosaki-senpai!

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:29.590
Why are you...

00:13:29.590 --> 00:13:35.280
I-I heard you moaning 
as I was walking by, and...

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:38.490
Sorry.

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:45.050
Um... Are you all right?

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:46.840
You don't look well.

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:49.300
It's nothing.

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:52.340
Kurosaki-senpai, I think 
you've been pushing yourself too—

00:13:52.340 --> 00:13:53.470
I'm not.

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.350
Um, I...

00:13:57.960 --> 00:13:58.820
What?

00:13:59.430 --> 00:14:03.280
Are you really not appearing 
in the last rock festival?

00:14:03.620 --> 00:14:05.830
I said I have work.

00:14:13.180 --> 00:14:18.840
Even if you can't play, you might be able 
to see some of it if you hurry there after work.

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:20.330
I'm not going.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:21.210
I told you.

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:26.170
Are you sure you don't actually want to go?

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:31.380
I-I'm sorry for being so presumptuous.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:32.720
But I...

00:14:33.770 --> 00:14:37.430
I can't forgive myself!

00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:38.810
What?

00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:45.230
When my friend asked 
if I'd play with him again...

00:14:45.230 --> 00:14:46.220
What?

00:14:46.220 --> 00:14:48.260
Do you want to get the band back together?

00:14:49.860 --> 00:14:51.320
Back together?

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:55.250
Yeah. Won't you stand with us on that stage?

00:14:55.780 --> 00:15:02.460
Maybe I'm being selfish, 
but I want to play with you one last time!

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:12.790
I wanted to go.

00:15:12.790 --> 00:15:18.100
I have work, but I wanted to stand 
on that stage at the festival!

00:15:18.100 --> 00:15:19.100
Then...

00:15:19.320 --> 00:15:20.600
But that's not good enough!

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:28.130
Now that we're entering the Triple S, 
I have more QUARTET NIGHT work than ever.

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:31.990
This is the stage where I belong now.

00:15:35.620 --> 00:15:37.510
I didn't understand back then.

00:15:40.130 --> 00:15:46.760
When the band broke up, 
I didn't understand why it always happened.

00:15:47.360 --> 00:15:49.510
I was just frustrated.

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:57.560
But my dad invited me to join the agency, 
and I became part of QUARTET NIGHT.

00:15:58.440 --> 00:16:00.190
Since meeting you guys...

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:02.170
...I finally understand what wasn't working.

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:05.610
So I won't make that mistake this time.

00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:08.560
I can't lose my place now.

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:19.150
To become an idol, 
I will give up rock... and my past.

00:16:45.220 --> 00:16:46.770
<i>I won't make that mistake this time.</i>

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:48.690
<i>I can't lose my place now.</i>

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:53.290
<i>To become an idol, 
I will give up rock... and my past.</i>

00:17:20.530 --> 00:17:24.850
Let's give it everything we've got today!

00:17:27.720 --> 00:17:28.560
You're so gloomy.

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:30.980
What's wrong, Ran-Ran? You've got no energy!

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:32.310
Shut up.

00:17:32.310 --> 00:17:33.690
Be quiet.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.220
You noisy fool.

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:37.850
Aw...

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:40.660
You guys are mean!

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:42.290
Wait!

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:49.170
Excuse me! Please wait!

00:17:56.230 --> 00:17:58.890
Oh, good. I made it.

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:01.760
Why are you in such a hurry, kiddo?

00:18:03.320 --> 00:18:05.270
I had to give this to you.

00:18:08.390 --> 00:18:10.810
It's your solo song.

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:19.130
I think your rock-loving and idol sides 
are both part of who you are.

00:18:19.580 --> 00:18:23.240
You're here now because you love rock.

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:24.830
So...

00:18:25.620 --> 00:18:28.350
QUARTET NIGHT, we're ready for you.

00:18:47.530 --> 00:18:49.560
We're shooting with our instruments.

00:18:50.550 --> 00:18:52.520
I see. Not a bad idea.

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:55.750
These maracas are nice.

00:18:55.750 --> 00:18:57.530
They feel great in my hands.

00:19:05.460 --> 00:19:06.620
Is something wrong?

00:19:09.060 --> 00:19:09.570
No...

00:19:09.570 --> 00:19:11.010
This is nice.

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:11.910
Shut up.

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:13.130
Aw...

00:19:21.570 --> 00:19:29.380
<i>I think your rock-loving and idol sides 
are both part of who you are.</i>

00:19:29.390 --> 00:19:33.310
<i>You're here now because you love rock.</i>

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:35.630
<i>I hope we get to play here someday.</i>

00:19:35.630 --> 00:19:38.280
<i>We'll fill this place with fans.</i>

00:19:38.550 --> 00:19:40.650
<i>Someday we will!</i>

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:45.240
Here.

00:19:46.680 --> 00:19:47.490
Reiji...

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:50.960
You already know, don't you?

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:03.470
Kurosaki-senpai...

00:20:05.830 --> 00:20:06.680
Let's go.

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:08.600
Okay!

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:16.270
He seems okay now.

00:20:16.810 --> 00:20:19.320
It's just because he doesn't often worry.

00:20:20.290 --> 00:20:23.620
Now I won't have him holding me back.

00:20:24.650 --> 00:20:28.910
You say that, but you were worried about him.

00:20:40.760 --> 00:20:42.080
No...

00:20:42.550 --> 00:20:44.830
But we made it this far...

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:53.100
Shut up and listen.

00:21:35.060 --> 00:21:36.210
A song?

00:21:36.210 --> 00:21:37.350
This voice...

00:21:37.860 --> 00:21:39.780
It's coming from over there.

00:21:56.590 --> 00:21:58.930
Nice song. Sounds like Ran-chan.

00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:03.540
Jinguji-san, Hijirikawa-san.

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:20.900
You just wait!

00:22:21.430 --> 00:22:25.030
I'll show you something even more amazing!

00:24:06.710 --> 00:24:08.100
You had fun, huh?

00:24:08.100 --> 00:24:10.100
I see. See you later.

00:24:10.100 --> 00:24:11.300
Uta Pri.
